hls: a WebVTT segment read on from the one before starts a new block

A media playlist of WebVTT segments that is opened on its own (a VOD
subtitle sidecar, not a rendition of a master playlist, whose segments
read_subtitle_packet() opens one by one) is read as one byte stream: each
segment's data follows the previous one's. Each segment is a WebVTT file
of its own (RFC 8216, 3.5), and a file need not end in a blank line. When
it does not, the webvtt demuxer reads the next segment's "WEBVTT" and
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP= header lines as more lines of the last cue, which shows
them on screen; a file that ends without a newline even joins "WEBVTT" to
the cue's last line.

When a segment that follows another one starts as a WebVTT file (an
optional BOM, then "WEBVTT" alone or followed by a space, tab or line
end), put a blank line in front of it, so its header is a block of its
own, which the demuxer skips (or applies, with timestamp_map). Other
segment data (MPEG-TS, fMP4, ID3, ADTS) never starts that way and reads
as before. The flag is cleared where the playlist's read starts afresh
(a seek, a changed selection, a re-enable).

diff --git a/libavformat/hls.c b/libavformat/hls.c
--- a/libavformat/hls.c
+++ b/libavformat/hls.c
@@ -170,6 +170,9 @@ struct playlist {
